statement:
Let $p_1,\dots,p_n$ be a probability vector, that is $p_i \ge 0$ for every $i$ and $\sum_{i} p_i = 1$, and let $\ell_1,\dots,\ell_n \in \bbr$ satisfy $0 \le \ell_i \le 1$ for every $i$. Then for every $\eta \in \bbr$,
\[
  \sum_{i} p_i\, e^{-\eta\,\ell_i}
  \;\le\;
  1 - \bigl(1 - e^{-\eta}\bigr)\sum_{i} p_i\,\ell_i.
\]

